  "id": "Compound::DB00568 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Cinnarizine is shown to bind to Cyp2a6 and Cyp2c9, both of which participate in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. This suggests that Cinnarizine may inhibit the activity of these cytochrome P450 enzymes, which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. The shared pathway involving Cyp2d6, which is also part of the arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, indicates a potential mechanism by which Cinnarizine could influence Cyp2d6 function. The evidence suggests that Cinnarizine may act as a competitive inhibitor of Cyp2d6, thereby affecting the metabolism of arachidonic acid. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Cinnarizine and Cyp2d6, particularly through the shared role of these enzymes in arachidonic acid metabolism. The observed scores and pathway connections provide a plausible explanation for the potential pharmacological interaction between Cinnarizine and Cyp2d6.",
